@inherits LayoutComponentBase

<div class="flex h-screen flex-col bg-background" data-testid="start-window">
    <div class="flex h-11 flex-none items-center gap-2 border-b bg-card px-4" data-testid="startbar">
        <BrandMark />
        <span class="text-sm font-semibold" data-testid="wordmark">Chatur</span>
        <span class="flex-1"></span>
        @* UI Design "Screen: Start", region `startbar`: the wordmark, the signed-in user, light or dark. *@
        <AccountMenu />
        <ThemeToggle />
    </div>
    <AuthGate>
        @* [fix 2026-09-23] `recent-side` (flex-1) and `get-started` (a fixed w-96) sat in a row that
           never stacked, so below 640px `get-started` held its own 384px and squeezed `recent-side`
           down to a sliver — every word in it wrapped to its own line (UIDesign "Rules": a panel
           scrolls inside itself, no window scrolls sideways). Stacked below 640px instead.
           [fix 2026-10-02] Below 640px the window itself grew and scrolled (min-h-screen), so no box in
           it was cut off against the mockup; from 640px up each panel scrolls inside itself.
           [fix 2026-11-17] Below 640px the stacked panels now scroll inside the window's own body, never
           the document: with Open a file added (BRD-215) the stacked page outgrew a phone-height window
           and the document itself scrolled, outside the app shell's scroll container. *@
        <div class="flex min-h-0 flex-1 flex-col overflow-y-auto sm:flex-row sm:overflow-hidden">
            @Body
        </div>
    </AuthGate>
</div>
